# The matplotlib fallback renderer's preview tree (demos/render.sh).
# It mirrors the committed lane structure — renders-preview/renders/ —
# and is ignored ON PURPOSE: a fallback frame must be structurally
# uncommittable (#221; see demos/check_render_provenance.py).
demos/renders-preview/

# Cargo build artifacts of the workspace-excluded projects
benches/target/
demos/tour/target/
demos/wild/target/
tools/k-lint/target/
tools/tess-lint/target/
tools/tess-meter/target/
/target-*

# The demo-document gallery, when it is written into the SOURCE tree.
# `gallery::run` defaults its output directory to the relative path
# "gallery" (gallery.rs), so `cargo run -- gallery` from inside
# demos/tour/ lands here. That is build output: CI writes its own copy
# to demos/out/gallery (render.yml) for the viewer's acceptance probe,
# nothing in the repo reads this path, and no gate regenerates it.
#
# Ten such files WERE tracked for a while — swept into the merge
# 423e3672d by a `git add -A` during conflict resolution; neither parent
# had them. They went stale the moment a scene's document changed, which
# is what the heat sink's PlacedUnion migration then did to
# heatsink.pncad. Untracked and ignored instead of re-goldened: a
# tracked artifact that no generator maintains and no gate checks is the
# shape that rots unnoticed, and this one already had.
demos/tour/gallery/
